@props(title: text)
<article class="mx-auto min-h-[70vh] max-w-4xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-20"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-500" href="/">← Back to home</a><span class="mt-10 block text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-600">About the starter</span><h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-5xl">A simple place to start.</h1><p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">This is a NeoKit starter styled with Tailwind CSS. Use it as the starting point for a site, dashboard, or small web application.</p><div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3"><section class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5"><h2 class="font-semibold">Native server rendering</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Templates compile to Neo functions. Pages arrive as complete HTML.</p></section><section class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5"><h2 class="font-semibold">Standard Tailwind</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Default colors, spacing, typography utilities, and responsive breakpoints. Edit the classes to make it yours.</p></section><section class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5"><h2 class="font-semibold">Optional JavaScript</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">The counter and filter load small browser modules. This about page ships without JavaScript.</p></section></div><div class="mt-10 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 p-5 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">NeoKit is an experimental framework with typed pages and actions, nested layouts, native data libraries, client navigation, and static export. Explore the feature and authenticated dashboard examples for the supported profiles.</div></article>
